A||||18||Archie||Fire in the Hole (twice)||||6||
Z||000000||Archie||10-08-2000||08:22 PM||||We fired up 2 V-8 cars this weekend.<P>On Friday we fired up a black 85 GT with a TPI LM1 Automatic. As many know I prefer stick shift Fieros but it sure is fun, once in a while, to "Punch and Steer". This thing bangs thru the gears very well indeed. Saturday we delivered the car to the customer in DesMoines, IA. So you IA residents better not challenge any faded black '85 GT's for a while.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-883s.jpg"> <P>While we are talking about firing up V-8 cars, I'd like to tell you that just this afternoon we booted up our new "Swap-Meet & Fiero Tow car".<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-900s.jpg"> <P>It's a 1984 Olds Cutless FWD Wagon. The engine is about 320 HP SBC, & all the original Olds P.Steering, A/C etc. are hooked up. This is Fiero related because the Olds uses the same 125-C transmission as the Fiero  & most of my Automatic V-8 kit parts work in this car too. And it's Fiero related because the SBC engine would have gone into a Fiero if the Olds hadn't got in the way.<P>Archie||||reg||6
Z||000001||Loki||10-08-2000||08:52 PM||||So Archie, what about delivering a car to Texas   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Loki||||reg||1
Z||000002||BOILERMAKER||10-08-2000||09:10 PM||||Could there be any better picture than a V-8 in a Fiero?  Please excuse me while I wipe the drool from the chin.||||reg||1
Z||000003||My7Fieros||10-08-2000||09:21 PM||||God that thing looks like a nightmare to work on lol....looks sweet though. I imagine there will be many unsuspecting vehicles that fall prey to that thing!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Archie||10-08-2000||10:03 PM||||As you can see there is actually plenty of room to work on the SBC in the Fiero engine compartment.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-888s.jpg"> <P>Besides, IMHO, the new SBC will need much less maintenance than the old used stock Fiero engine.<P>The Olds engine compartment is just a bit tight on the back side of the engine, what with the PS rack, heater box etc. back there. But you could still change the plugs without too much trouble.<P>Archie||||reg||1
